# N4 (lmx.h.lm1 M.parent; LMX_semantics.ru.md #fields: node is the lexical space above the method): node in the
# code is the parent of the code, not the space of its caller. S and D sit at the unit, where k is 5; the call runs
# in m, where k is 40. S writes node\k + 2 into the x of D: 7, not 42. With unit_n4_split_node_code_parent (the
# data is local to the caller there) this pins node = code\parent against the caller and the data. Entry 7.
int: k 5
D:
    int: x 0
end: D
S:
    int: x
    x: node\k + 2
end: S
fn: m () int
    int: k 40
    call: S D
    return: D\x
end: m
int: got m()
int: r 81
if: got = 7 && D\x = 7
    r: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
